#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example shows an E-Class sedan driving over a small bump with the MF-Swift (Short Wavelength) tire model.
#
#Because this type of simulation involves higher frequencies, the output file is updated every time step: 0.001 sec (1000 Hz).
#
#This example is overlaid with other two simulations: "MF-Tyre, Sym.: Small Bump" (red vehicle) "Extended Tires: Small Bump" (blue vehicle)
#
#Each vehicle uses a different tire model, although all three are based on the same tire characteristics.
#
#An MF-Swift Tire license is required from TNO/TASS to run the math model for this example. However, you can still view the simulation results provided with CarSim by clicking the "Video" and "Plot" buttons.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

